# Dusk Over Dunmere, by MiMo v2.6 Pro and SZ. An original for the Chiptune style: a slow 3/4
# fantasy RPG theme for an old town at dusk, heroic but lonely. The pulse lead sings a long,
# held-note melody in D minor (leaning on D Dorian, with a bright B natural over the G chord in
# bar 14 of the theme); rolling pulse-arp broken chords drive it in place of drums; the triangle
# bass walks under them; a square counter-melody answers the lead in its held bars from the second
# statement on; square pad chords hold the bigger moments; the noise kit plays only in the B
# section (soft hats, then a light march snare). Form: arp-only intro, theme A, theme A with the
# counter, a lift to F major that builds, a quiet bridge of just arp and bass that ends on a
# dominant B, theme A up a step in E minor with everything, and an outro that ritards down to the
# lone arp. The theme's chords are Dm Dm Bb F Gm Dm C Am | Bb F Gm Dm Bb G Am Am; the bridge is
# Dm Dm Bb Gm C Am Bb B; everything from the last statement on is those chords up a step.
title: Dusk Over Dunmere
composer: MiMo v2.6 Pro & SZ
about: A wistful 3/4 world-map theme at dusk: a singing pulse lead over rolling arpeggios, one last look back up a step in E minor.
year: 2026
source: original
category: originals
style: chiptune
key: D minor
tempo: 88
time: 3/4

# A slight ritardando through the outro, stepped like a player winding down.
@bar 83 tempo=84
@bar 85 tempo=76
@bar 86 tempo=68
@bar 87 tempo=58
@bar 88 tempo=48

